{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>טמא (tamei)</b> — two times in the Masorah: and the other is למען טמא את מקדשי. Hint to a zar (non-priest) who served — he is stricken with tzara'at. That is, למען טמא את מקדשי — a zar who enters to perform avodah defiles it. And that is what is written of Uzziah: ובידו מקטרת להקטיר והצרעת זרחה במצחו." "<b>נגעו</b> — two times in the Masorah: and the other is אשר ידע איש את נגעו, regarding the matter of Solomon's prayer. That is, at the beginning of the matter — בראשו נגעו — one must know his affliction and cleanse himself of it through teshuvah before praying."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The phrase למען טמא את מקדשי (Numbers 19:20) and the Uzziah citation (II Chronicles 26:19) are unaddressed in the source.", 1 "The phrase אשר ידע איש את נגעו (Leviticus 13:9) is unaddressed in the source. The allusion to Solomon's prayer likely refers to I Kings 8:38."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:22.727834589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}